---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const privacyContact = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL?.trim();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Aflora handles newsletter consent and delivery data."
  translations={{ en: "/privacy", "pt-BR": "/pt-br/privacy" }}
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Last updated · July 28, 2026</p>
    <h1>Privacy at Aflora</h1>
    <p class="lede">The newsletter collects only what is needed to confirm consent, deliver each issue, and understand whether delivery is healthy.</p>
  </header>

  <article class="lesson-body policy-page">
    <h2>What the newsletter stores</h2>
    <p>When you request a subscription, Aflora stores your email address, language, signup source, optional campaign parameters, and consent timestamps in PostgreSQL. Your subscription stays pending until you use the time-limited confirmation link.</p>
    <p>The signup service uses your network address briefly for in-memory rate limiting. It is not written to the subscriber or analytics tables.</p>

    <h2>Delivery providers and measurement</h2>
    <p>Confirmed addresses are synchronized to Resend, which sends confirmation messages and newsletter issues. Railway hosts the website, API, and PostgreSQL database.</p>
    <p>Signed Resend webhooks report sends, deliveries, opens, clicks, bounces, complaints, suppressions, and subscription changes. The analytics table stores a keyed recipient hash—not the email address—along with the event type, time, broadcast id, and clicked URL when applicable. Opens can be distorted by privacy proxies and image blocking.</p>

    <h2>Optional readership measurement</h2>
    <p>Aflora does not measure your reading activity unless you accept the measurement prompt. If you accept, Aflora creates a random browser identifier and records page views, active foreground reading time, scroll completion, broad device class, locale, campaign parameters, learning-lab starts, selected calls to action, browser performance, and sanitized error categories.</p>
    <p>Aflora does not store your network address, full browser signature, typed text, pointer movements, or a replay of the page. External referrals are reduced to the referring hostname; same-site referrals retain only the path.</p>
    <p>If you confirm a newsletter subscription in a browser that has accepted measurement, a short-lived, single-use token may connect that browser identifier to your subscriber id. The token contains no email address and does not recognize you across other browsers or devices.</p>

    <h2>Retention and control</h2>
    <p>Unconfirmed requests older than 30 days, delivery events older than 400 days, and person-level readership activity older than 400 days are deleted under the retention process. Before old readership records are removed, non-identifying daily article totals may be retained. Consent and suppression records are retained to document permission and prevent unwanted future delivery. Every issue includes an unsubscribe link.</p>
    <p>Use the “Measurement settings” control on any page to reject or withdraw analytics. Withdrawal stops collection, removes the browser identifier, and requests deletion of its person-level activity. Newsletter subscription and analytics consent are independent.</p>
    <p>You may ask to access or delete your data. Verified deletion requests may retain the minimum suppression record needed to ensure Aflora does not email the address again.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    {privacyContact ? (
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${privacyContact}`}>{privacyContact}</a> with privacy questions or requests.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>The operator must configure a public privacy contact before newsletter signup can be enabled.</p>
    )}
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
